From 97c0a9248d87e746968d665948244063425fb5ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marouene Boubakri <marouene.boubakri@nxp.com>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 23:50:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] IIOTSOL1-1626: Serialise SE05x access across processes with
 flock

EVerest runs each module as a separate process. With multiple modules
loading nxp_prov (EvseSecurity, EvseV2G, IsoMux), each process has
its own libsssProvider.so mapping, its own gProvider_boot_ctx, and
opens its own SSS session against /dev/i2c-0. Concurrent T=1
transactions from different processes interleave on the bus and
surface as phNxpEseProto7816_CheckCRC failures and SM_I2CConnect
status 7002 at OSSL_provider_init.

Userspace mutexes don't cross PID boundaries. Use flock() on a shared
lock file so all processes serialise on the same kernel-managed
advisory lock for the duration of each SSS transaction.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Marouene Boubakri <marouene.boubakri@nxp.com>
---
 provider/sssProvider_ecdsa.c | 25 ++++++++++++++++-
 provider/sssProvider_main.c  | 53 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 provider/sssProvider_main.h  |  4 +++
 provider/sssProvider_store.c |  5 ++++
 4 files changed, 86 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

